{"text":"Whole-outcome correction replacing unclaimed d226be30 for audit55563589/reviewf24d2b56. Builder: gate public founding and unbound room IDs (simplification review 55563589, findings SEC-03, SEC-06, COST-02). POST /v1/rooms and /found need no credential and have no limit (room/src/http.ts:82-87); each founding can create a repository, Room storage and registry binding; the first commit uses direct smart HTTP and Publisher startup follows publication work; the idle-loop repair3da1d82b is already landed, so no unsupported monthly per-room bill is asserted, so a scripted stranger can create unbounded recurring cost and exhaust the account's container capacity. Any room-ID-shaped path also instantiates a Room object and writes its schema without consulting the registry (http.ts:37-45; core.ts createSchema in the constructor). Names bind first-come forever with no normalisation (founding.ts:45-49; registry.ts:67-79), so look-alikes of real rooms can be squatted. Required: (1) a founding gate, which is hugh's decision (see the decisions assert): an operator-signed grant for every founding, or a per-address quota with a Rate Limiting binding, or proof of work; (2) roomStub resolves IDs through the registry and returns not-found before ROOMS.get for unbound IDs; (3) names restricted to a normalised printable set with confusables refused; (4) createdAt bounded to the room clock. Start after hugh's decision on the gate. OwnerD1 remains deferred to complete control-Rooms/firm-auth design34cf/d50ce26d; do not choose founding authority here. Retain eventual owner-decided gate, registry-before-object, normalized printable/confusable names and room-clock createdAt bounds. Quantify operator exposure with actual provider operations/storage/duration and account-wide quotas; do not infer CPU-first capacity or recurring container cost from founding alone. Reviewed main base 344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482; historical sources were93a2552e/a6330262. Acts enabling jam remain first, followed by necessary jam-task spikes, then jam and the full Artroom docs in parallel (user7363396b/04da4388). No blanket before-J2/J3/public-deployment or empty-backlog readiness gate and no deployment are added.","body":{"conditions":"Founding is gated as decided; an unbound room ID creates no object; a confusable or control-character name is refused; tests for each; docs/protocol.md R-GEN-10 to R-GEN-13 amended; root gates pass; checker review. D1 approval is a dependency of the founding-gate design, not permission supplied by this correction.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8592926f1d4d30e3cf282eadc411dacde51d3ac0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a3bbf8f3b7ccc7ba4fd596a6bcfe5756d51a77e","target_head":"344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d226be307f524d35944b161491749f0efb4651a4","retirement":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e6c994ea9787dba38863fd4e18f60acc3fd57165","promise":"absent","completion":"absent"}}